# Fixed-source clean candidate: host preparation only

`candidate_manifest.py` hashes the already saved candidate files, validates the
original vendor tar member-by-member, decompresses the pinned pristine gzip to an
automatically removed **host temporary file**, and reads selected ext4 metadata
and files. It never mounts an image, starts a VM, imports a device backend, runs
firmware, sends ADB/SSH/AT, or modifies input files. There is no live execute API.

The candidate is the existing local build from source commit
`569f13d4ce15585f70817c2a1e03bb574a84720b`, including the already reviewed
`boot/init` diagnostic `count=1024` cap and upstream mobile4 kernel adaptations.
It is **not an upstream release binary** and does not add W1, D1 or OpenClash.

The generated schema is `e5-clean-author-candidate-v1`. `artifacts` contains fixed
absolute paths, lengths and SHA-256; `attestation` is limited to the precise
pristine rootfs. All `pending_live_gates` stay pending and
`approved_for_device_execution` is false. The file is not an installer request.

```
python3 -B tools/e5_clean_author_prepare_20261014/candidate_manifest.py --output <new-host-json-path>
python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tools/e5_clean_author_prepare_20261014 -p test_candidate_manifest.py -v
```

Output creation is exclusive. A previous result is not silently replaced. The
ext4 reader is intentionally limited, rejects unsupported/unknown layouts, and
is used only after both compressed and full uncompressed SHA/size match fixed
pins. These are host tests and artifact checks, not hardware acceptance.

## File selection and default boot

The proposed new active directory has **eight initial files**:

| File | Source |
|---|---|
| `boot.img` | Pinned 64 MiB boot; SHA `153af211…` |
| `openwrt.ext4.gz` | Pinned pristine gzip; SHA `7aa7c714…` |
| `openwrt.ext4` | Exact 2 GiB decompression; SHA `d96c0623…` |
| `device-files.tar` | Existing own-device collection; SHA `e61d64b5…` |
| `openwrt-install.conf` | Existing pinned settings, `E5_DEFAULT_BOOT='android'`; values stay private |
| `fscrypt-probe` | Pinned probe copied from `fscrypt-policy-probe`; it is not executed by this tool |
| `boot-os` | Literal `openwrt\n`: select this Linux rootfs for a B trial |
| `openwrt-default-boot` | Literal `android\n`: return to Android by default |

`boot-os=openwrt` does not mean persistent default-Linux. The clean image has no
inner Linux default marker, and the fixed `92-e5-default-boot` script only changes
the default for an explicit Linux setting. `90-e5` imports the outer settings
into `/etc/e5/install.conf` and removes the outer settings file during first boot;
the later normal directory therefore may have seven files. Do not copy a stale
`boot-os-next`, `.new` image, hash sidecar, old configuration, or pending update.
The transaction must preserve the old directory separately rather than merge it.

## Vendor and fresh NV initialization

The pristine image has an empty `/opt/e5/android` and no `/opt/e5/nv`, previous
`factory-sha256.json`, install configuration, device-files stamp, or default boot
marker. `boot/init` takes the own-device archive from the active outer directory,
loads early firmware, and injects vendor files before `switch_root`. That archive
contains runtime/WCN/GNSS/audio files, not NR partition images or private NV.

At the first boot of the **new** image, S20 `e5-vendor` invokes
`t551m-nv-prepare` before vendor processes. The program protects the nine actual
physical NV partitions, records their hashes, initializes isolated working
copies, reconciles valid primary/backup working pairs if necessary, and binds
loop devices. The old image's working NV and origin must never be imported.
Subsequent vendor writes may change working copies; their later equality to the
physical source is not a valid universal requirement.

The future operator still needs the immediate preboot physical-nine baseline,
first-boot origin and read-only flags, exact geometry, loop mappings and
`t551m-nv-verify`, followed by physical hashes. This candidate does not create that
evidence or declare it passed. Preserve the old image for review and rollback;
do not run `--refresh` against it as part of this candidate preparation.

## Remaining gates

Actual free space, current A/root/boot ID, no-SIM cold observation and AP panic
risk review, B/misc/GPT/protected preimages, inactive directory and loop/open-file
checks, whole old-directory backup, safe directory switch, slot switching and
rollback remain separate reviewed operations. Existing frozen first-install
code rejects an already present active directory; this tool never bypasses it.
No addresses, available-space observations or fresh device hashes are invented.
